# Supabase project the app talks to. For a local stack, start it with
# `npx supabase start` and read both values from `npx supabase status`
# (API URL and anon key).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# The key the app still sends with no JWT. Since 20261102150000_add_user_ownership.sql
# revokes anon's grants on both tables, it only reaches Auth (sign up / sign in);
# it reads no data, so an anonymous visitor sees the sign-in screen, not the log.
# Paste a value, do not leave this blank: createClient() refuses an empty key with
# `supabaseKey is required`. The test suite reads neither value - src/__tests__/setup.ts
# replaces the client outright (2026-11-03), so CI passes without an .env at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
